output:
While PHP can help with some basic grammar rules, it is not designed to fully correct verb tenses and other complex grammar rules. However, there are some libraries and APIs available that can assist with this task. One such library is the LanguageTool API.
You can use the LanguageTool API to check the grammar of your text and suggest corrections. Here is an example code snippet that demonstrates how to use the LanguageTool API to correct the grammar of your text:
```
$text = "i had wrote down my thoughts";
// Send a request to the LanguageTool API
$url = 'https://languagetool.org/api/v2/check';
$data = array(
    'text' => $text,
    'language' => 'en-US'
);
$options = array(
    'http' => array(
        'header'  => "Content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\r\n",
        'method'  => 'POST',
        'content' => http_build_query($data),
    ),
);
$context  = stream_context_create($options);
$result = file_get_contents($url, false, $context);
// Parse the response and get the corrected text
$xml = simplexml_load_string($result);
$fixedText = $xml->matches->match->replacements->replacement->__toString();
// Output the corrected text
echo $fixedText;
```
This code sends a request to the LanguageTool API with your text and language information. The API then returns a response with suggested corrections. The code then extracts the corrected text from the response and outputs it.
Note that the LanguageTool API has some limitations and may not catch all grammar errors. It is also important to note that automated grammar correction may not always be perfect and it is always a good idea to double-check the corrected text manually.

