As a software developer, you need to create a password with specific criteria. The password must contain exactly 10 characters and have the following properties:
- The first character must be a letter from A to Z (uppercase or lowercase).
- The second character must be a digit from 0 to 9.
- The third character must be a symbol from !, @, #, $, %, ^, &, or *.
- The fourth character must be a letter from A to Z (uppercase or lowercase), but it cannot be the same as the first character.
- The fifth character must be a digit from 0 to 9, but it cannot be the same as the second character.
- The sixth character must be a symbol from !, @, #, $, %, ^, &, or *, but it cannot be the same as the third character.
- The seventh character must be a letter from A to Z (uppercase or lowercase), but it cannot be the same as the first or fourth character.
- The eighth character must be a digit from 0 to 9, but it cannot be the same as the second or fifth character.
- The ninth character must be a symbol from !, @, #, $, %, ^, &, or *, but it cannot be the same as the third or sixth character.
- The tenth character must be a letter from A to Z (uppercase or lowercase), but it cannot be the same as the first, fourth, or seventh character.
What is the probability of generating such a password that contains exactly 3 digits and 4 uppercase letters?
[Scala code]:
val digits = "0123456789"
val symbols = "!@#$%^&*"
val uppercase = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"
def generatePassword(): String = {
  val firstChar = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
  val secondChar = digits(util.Random.nextInt(10))
  val thirdChar = symbols(util.Random.nextInt(9))
  val fourthChar = {
    var temp = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
    while (temp == firstChar) {
      temp = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
    }
    temp
  }
  val fifthChar = {
    var temp = digits(util.Random.nextInt(10))
    while (temp == secondChar) {
      temp = digits(util.Random.nextInt(10))
    }
    temp
  }
  val sixthChar = {
    var temp = symbols(util.Random.nextInt(9))
    while (temp == thirdChar) {
      temp = symbols(util.Random.nextInt(9))
    }
    temp
  }
  val seventhChar = {
    var temp = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
    while (temp == firstChar || temp == fourthChar) {
      temp = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
    }
    temp
  }
  val eighthChar = {
    var temp = digits(util.Random.nextInt(10))
    while (temp == secondChar || temp == fifthChar) {
      temp = digits(util.Random.nextInt(10))
    }
    temp
  }
  val ninthChar = {
    var temp = symbols(util.Random.nextInt(9))
    while (temp == thirdChar || temp == sixthChar) {
      temp = symbols(util.Random.nextInt(9))
    }
    temp
  }
  val tenthChar = {
    var temp = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
    while (temp == firstChar || temp == fourthChar || temp == seventhChar) {
      temp = uppercase(util.Random.nextInt(26))
    }
    temp
  }

  firstChar.toString + secondChar.toString + thirdChar.toString +
  fourthChar.toString + fifthChar.toString + sixthChar.toString +
  seventhChar.toString + eighthChar.toString + ninthChar.toString +
  tenthChar.toString
}
val numTries = 100000
var count = 0
for (i <- 1 to numTries) {
  val password = generatePassword()
  val numDigits = password.filter(_.isDigit).length
  val numUppercase = password.filter(_.isUpper).length
  if (numDigits == 3 && numUppercase == 4) {
    count += 1
  }
}
val probability = count.toDouble / numTries.toDouble
println(s"The probability of generating such a password is $probability")

