How can we develop a more robust PHP function that leverages multiple APIs to translate complex English statements into Spanish, considering grammatical tense and gender agreement? The function should allow for specification of the dog's breed, age, and size, as well as any relevant contextual information about the barking (e.g. duration and frequency). Additionally, the function should account for regional variations in Spanish and provide options for choosing between different dialects. Here is an example PHP function that integrates Google Translate API, Watson Language Translator API, and Amazon Polly API to translate and vocalize the statement:
```php
function translate_and_speak($text, $known, $breed, $age, $size, $gender, $context, $duration, $frequency, $dialect) {
  $google_url = 'https://translation.googleapis.com/language/translate/v2';
  $google_data = array(
    'q' => $text,
    'source' => 'en',
    'target' => 'es',
    'format' => 'text',
    'model' => 'base',
    'key' => 'YOUR_GOOGLE_API_KEY_HERE'
  );
  $google_options = array(
    'http' => array(
      'header'  => "Content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\r\n",
      'method'  => 'POST',
      'content' => http_build_query($google_data),
    ),
  );
  $google_context  = stream_context_create($google_options);
  $google_result = json_decode(file_get_contents($google_url, false, $google_context));
  $google_translation = $google_result->data->translations[0]->translatedText;

  $watson_url = 'https://api.us-south.language-translator.watson.cloud.ibm.com/instances/YOUR_WATSON_INSTANCE_ID_HERE/v3/translate?version=2018-05-01';
  $watson_data = array(
    'text' => array($text),
    'source' => 'en',
    'target' => 'es'
  );
  $watson_options = array(
    'http' => array(
      'header'  => "Content-type: application/json\r\nAuthorization: Basic " . base64_encode("apikey:" . "YOUR_WATSON_API_KEY_HERE") . "\r\n",
      'method'  => 'POST',
      'content' => json_encode($watson_data),
    ),
  );
  $watson_context  = stream_context_create($watson_options);
  $watson_result = json_decode(file_get_contents($watson_url, false, $watson_context));
  $watson_translation = $watson_result->translations[0]->translation;

  $polly_url = 'https://YOUR_AWS_REGION.amazonaws.com/polly/v1/speech';
  $polly_data = array(
    'Text' => $google_translation,
    'OutputFormat' => 'mp3',
    'VoiceId' => 'YOUR_AWS_VOICE_ID_HERE'
  );
  $polly_options = array(
    'http' => array(
      'header'  => "Content-type: application/json\r\nAuthorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential=YOUR_AWS_CREDENTIALS_HERE,SignedHeaders=content-type;host;x-amz-date;x-amz-target,Signature=YOUR_AWS_SIGNATURE_HERE\r\nX-Amz-Target: Polly.SynthesizeSpeech\r\nX-Amz-Date: " . gmdate("Ymd\THis\Z") . "\r\nHost: polly." . $aws_region . ".amazonaws.com\r\n",
      'method'  => 'POST',
      'content' => json_encode($polly_data),
    ),
  );
  $polly_context  = stream_context_create($polly_options);
  $polly_result = file_get_contents($polly_url, false, $polly_context);

  if ($known) {
    if ($breed == 'golden retriever') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('el perro', 'el golden retriever', $google_translation);
    } else if ($breed == 'chihuahua') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('el perro', 'el chihuahua', $google_translation);
    }
    if ($gender == 'male') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('el', 'él', $google_translation);
    } else if ($gender == 'female') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('la', 'ella', $google_translation);
    }
  } else {
    if ($size == 'small') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('un perro', 'un perrito', $google_translation);
    } else if ($size == 'large') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('un perro', 'un gran perro', $google_translation);
    }
    if ($gender == 'male') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('un', 'un macho', $google_translation);
    } else if ($gender == 'female') {
      $google_translation = str_replace('una', 'una hembra', $google_translation);
    }
  }

  if ($dialect == 'mexican') {
    $google_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando wey', $google_translation);
    $watson_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando güey', $watson_translation);
  } else if ($dialect == 'spanish') {
    $google_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando tío', $google_translation);
    $watson_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando amigo', $watson_translation);
  }

  if ($duration == 'long') {
    $google_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando sin parar', $google_translation);
    $watson_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando continuamente', $watson_translation);
  } else if ($duration == 'short') {
    $google_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando brevemente', $google_translation);
    $watson_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando por un momento', $watson_translation);
  }

  if ($frequency == 'frequent') {
    $google_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando constantemente', $google_translation);
    $watson_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando repetidamente', $watson_translation);
  } else if ($frequency == 'infrequent') {
    $google_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando ocasionalmente', $google_translation);
    $watson_translation = str_replace('está ladrando', 'está ladrando de vez en cuando', $watson_translation);
  }

  return array($google_translation, $watson_translation, $polly_result);
}
```
The function takes in the English statement as a parameter, as well as various parameters related to the dog and context of barking. It then leverages multiple APIs to translate and vocalize the statement in Spanish, with options for choosing between different dialects and modifying the translation based on the provided parameters. To use the function, simply call it with the appropriate parameters, like this:
