How can I find all pairs of numbers in the given list of integers whose absolute difference is equal to the target number and sort them in ascending order based on the first number in the pair using PHP? Also, how can I make sure that there are no duplicate pairs included in the result?
Here is the PHP code that can achieve this:
$list = array(7, 4, 2, 1, 9, 8);
$target = 4;
sort($list);
$result = array();
for($i=0; $i<count($list)-1; $i++){
    for($j=$i+1; $j<count($list); $j++){
        if(abs($list[$i]-$list[$j])==$target){
            $pair = array($list[$i], $list[$j]);
            if(!in_array($pair, $result)){
                array_push($result, $pair);
            }
        }
    }
}
//sort result in ascending order based on the first number in the pair
usort($result, function($a, $b) {
    return $a[0] - $b[0];
});
//print the result
foreach($result as $pair){
    echo "(".$pair[0].", ".$pair[1].") ";
}

