To find the 25th term of the given arithmetic sequence, we can use the formula:
an = a1 + (n-1)d
where,
an = nth term of the sequence
a1 = first term of the sequence
d = common difference between the terms
n = value of n (in this case, n = 25)
Substituting the given values, we get:
a25 = 2 + (25-1)4
a25 = 2 + 96
a25 = 98
Therefore, the 25th term of the given arithmetic sequence is 98.
Here's a Java program to find the nth term of an arithmetic sequence:
```
import java.util.Scanner;
public class ArithmeticSequence {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the first term: ");
        int a1 = input.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter the common difference: ");
        int d = input.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter the value of n: ");
        int n = input.nextInt();
        int an = a1 + (n-1)*d;
        System.out.println("The " + n + "th term of the arithmetic sequence is: " + an);
    }
}
```
