	<p>The Schlieffen Plan also had an impact on the policies of other nations. France and Great Britain were alarmed by the plan and saw it as a threat to their security. France began to fortify its border with Germany, and Great Britain began to build up its navy to counter the threat from Germany. Russia also saw the plan as a threat and began to mobilize its army in response.</p>

