Once we've estimated the model, we can use it to simulate the impact of different economic scenarios on the market. For example, we can simulate what would happen to stock prices if GDP were to increase by 1%:
```matlab
% Simulate response to GDP shock
shock = zeros(1, size(y,2));
shock(2) = 0.01; % GDP shock
response = simulate(model, 10, 'numPaths', 1000, 'initial', y(end,:), 'shocks', shock);
% Plot results
figure;
plot(response(:,1));
title('Response of Stock Prices to 1% Increase in GDP');
ylabel('Stock Prices');
xlabel('Time (quarters)');
```
In this code, we're simulating the VAR model for 10 quarters with 1000 paths and an initial condition of the last observation in the data. We're also specifying a shock to the second variable (GDP) of 1%. Finally, we're plotting the response of stock prices to this shock.
